{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794308453,"nonce":"LNsAL9qqV9DqynfpTwoaJD1IQg4=","message":"Ceiling for a direct AIR-to-wasm backend, from stage timings of two -O3 preview-config builds (Pocket Studio bytecode, macOS, load ~1.4-2.1, fiber transform off in these runs): wall 8.5-9.3 s = llvm_ir 2.2-2.6 s + llvm_backend 5.7-5.9 s + fixed stages ~0.9 s (decode 0.03, module_setup 0.2, wasm inputs/resolve/layout/relocs/emit ~0.4, link 0.4). With the fiber transform on (RayDE preview) earlier runs added ~0.65 s and a link of ~1.05 s, so the fixed floor is ~1.3-2.4 s. A backend that replaced LLVM entirely would therefore take the build from ~8.5-9 s to about 1.5-2.5 s plus its own emit time: a ceiling of roughly 6 s (~70%) per edit, before any emitter cost. Not an estimate of the real saving: it needs the emit-only prototype from the plan (P0 census, then time emitting all 2,699 functions without running them).","files":null}]}